From 27f222b55b348edfe977818f5af7eba744b1c93a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Workbench-Agent <workbench-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:47:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(tests): derive authorization timestamps from current
 UTC clock

The stale fixed-clock fixtures in test_effect_gateway.py, test_operations.py
and test_final_gate.py hard-coded 2026-08-21 12:00 UTC, which causes every
human-authorization test to fail when run later because the current wall
clock is no longer inside [approved_at, expires_at].

Derive _utc() from datetime.now(timezone.utc) so the positive fixtures stay
valid indefinitely. The explicit expired-authorization fixture in
test_effect_gateway.py still passes hours_valid=-1 to keep the negative
behavior intact.

Phase 0 Runtime gate step: 43/43 focused tests pass; full pytest 333/333
pass with no other modifications.
